  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who All-Star Movies is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families watching the nightly rate.</strong> This is one of the lowest-priced Disney-owned resorts at Walt Disney World. In 2026 a Standard Room ran about $153 to $311 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>Parties of four who can live with a Value room.</strong> A queen bed and a queen-size table bed (a Murphy bed that folds down from a table) is the usual setup.</li>
      <li><strong>Anyone fine with a food court and a bus.</strong> That's the whole transportation and dining picture here.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You want a sit-down restaurant at the hotel.</strong> There's a food court and a pool bar, and that's it.</li>
      <li><strong>You want Extended Evening Hours.</strong> Value resort guests don't get them.</li>
      <li><strong>You're staying through January 2027 and you're sensitive to construction.</strong> Official pages say guest rooms are under planned refurbishment through January 2027. You may see or hear work, and alternate walkways may be in place. The resort stays open.</li>
      <li><strong>You don't want to walk.</strong> Book a Preferred room, which sits closer to Cinema Hall. Standard rooms can be a longer walk with a stroller or tired kids.</li>
    </ul>
