    <p class="note">Categories, beds, occupancy and the Preferred-location note come from Disney's official room listings and from MouseSavers' October 2026 compilation of Disney's rate categories. The 260 sq ft figure comes from a Disney travel-agent overview. Sq ft per guest is our math, using 260 divided by 4. MouseSavers also notes that a single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum <span class="verify">[verify still current]</span>. Official amenity listings for these rooms include free Wi-Fi, a beverage cooler, a coffee machine, an in-room safe, a hairdryer and an iron.</p>
    <h3>What's in the room</h3>
    <p>The queen-size table bed folds down from a table, which frees floor space during the day if you put it back up. A king room will not sleep four the same way. Rooms are under refurbishment through January 2027, so the finishes you get may depend on when you stay <span class="verify">[verify current in-room look]</span>.</p>
    <p>Accessible rooms exist, but we haven't confirmed their layouts or bed options yet <span class="verify">[verify]</span>.</p>
